at five las vegas raiders star henry  ruggs arrested accused of a fiery and  deadly dui crash the latest from the  scene and reaction from the raiders  breaking his silence superintendent  jesus jarrah issue in the first  statement since his firing his message  for teachers  76 degrees weather now winds are calm as  well and cooler than yesterday we'll  have more on your forecast straight  ahead  this is an eight news now breaking news  alert  we are following breaking news here off  the top at five a las vegas raiders star  accused of causing a deadly crash on a  local road this video from a neighbor  shows the fiery aftermath early this  morning  this news reaching around the world  today cutting through the sporting world  and the las vegas community and good  evening to you thank you for joining us  on eight news now at five i'm brian  loftis and i'm denise valdez we have  team coverage tonight joe moeller has a  closer look at henry ruggs the young man  accused in that crash chris matthews has  reaction from the raiders but we start  with victoria saha with what we've  learned about this tragic crash victoria  the roads here are back open it took  police more than 12 hours to examine the  scene and take the person who died out  of one of those burning cars  and we are learning that she was a 23  year old person now this early morning  crash shook up this whole neighborhood  metro police confirmed ruggs was driving  his chevrolet corvette when he hit a  toyota rav4 the rav4 was traveling north  on south rainbow by spring valley in the  right lane at the same time police say  ruggs and a female passenger were in his  corvette going fast in the center lane  then veered off to the right lane that's  where the raft 4 was the front of rug's  car hit the rav4 from behind when the  rav4 came to a stop it caught on fire  when first responders got on scene they  found the driver of the raft four dead  she was 23 years old amy rigo lives  right in this area she provided 8 news  now with the video of the rav4 catching  fire i don't know if anybody had time to  take whoever was in there or what or  they were scared because you know corona  whatever but i really felt bad that  you know i feel like  maybe if somebody wasn't just not afraid  could have went out there and helped  them metro police say ruggs stayed on  scene after the crash and showed signs  of impairment he was taken to umc with  non-life-threatening injuries  ruggs was released from the hospital and  taken into the clark county detention  center he is due back in court in court  excuse me tomorrow morning at 9 00 a.m  victoria saha live local now  victoria thank you henry ruggs will be  charged with dui resulting in death now  in nevada that charge is a class b  felony it's punishable anywhere from two  to 20 years if ruggs is convicted rugs  could also be suspended by the nfl which  has a personal conduct and a substance  abuse policy rug's attorney david  chesnov and richard schoenfield have  asked the public to reserve judgment  until all the facts are gathered  meanwhile his teammates and victims  families will try to cope with this  tragedy sports director chris matthews  has more now on what the raiders are  saying this afternoon chris joining us  live in studio well thank you very much  brian football is so insignificant  during this time of tragedy it's hard to  imagine what's going on in the minds of  the players right now as they try to  prepare for a game this sunday raiders  headquarters parking lot was full of  cars this afternoon and one can only  imagine the conversations going on  behind the steel bars and inside that  facility shock over the player involved  in a preventable accident that took the  life of another human being it's no  longer about football we caught up with  former nfl quarterback randall  cunningham who is the pastor at remnant  ministries he's also the raiders team  chaplain  uh what's happened it's a tragedy uh but  we just gotta really be encouraging to  both families and yes he's got a little  girl so  um  you know as a pastor and as a chaplain  of the raiders i'm available to you know  just encourage them and encourage both  families  all right both families will need some  help certainly the raiders did release a  statement this morning which reads in  part we are devastated by the loss of  life and our thoughts and prayers go out  to the victims family we are in the  process of gathering information and  will have no further comment at this  time cunningham has had rugs over and  many other raiders over to his ministry  in the past he is also sending his  sincerest condolences to the victims  families denise chris thanks for that so  rugs of course facing some very serious  charges that could result in prison time  and fines and joe mohler continues our  team coverage from the clark county  detention center with more on what now  could be awaiting rugs  after being treated for those  non-life-threatening injuries a few  blocks from here at umc he was brought  to the detention center where he is now  officially charged with duin reckless  driving  in the state of nevada this is a class b  felony and rugs could face anywhere from  two to 20 years in jail metro did not  release specifics about ruggs's injuries  from the crash people have been reacting  to news of the crash since it broke this  morning clark county commissioner  michael naff took the twitter outrage  over what has happened he has been  outspoken about the fatal crashes  happening in the valley lately  i don't care who you are there's no  excuse for this kind of behavior even  more when every single person in our  community has the option to take public  transit if you're drinking if you're  abusing substances every single person  in our community has the opportunity to  call a friend everyone in our community  has the option to take advantage of ride  share services  you know back out here live many fans of  the raiders have been reacting on social  media as well many people expressing  their disappointment with a decision  that was allegedly made last night to  get behind the wheel many people saying  the same thing is naft saying there are  plenty of options out there to take a  safe drive or safe ride to get home  reporting live in downtown las vegas  john muller live local now  henry ruggs is the now 26th nfl player  arrested this year that's according to a  usa today database and of the 26 players  arrested in 2020 six were for dui three  members of the las vegas raiders have  been arrested including running back  josh jacobs for dui in january and  cornerback kima sivaron who was arrested  for evading in texas that was in  february now of course this arrest  coming at a very difficult time for the  team just last month head coach john  gruden caught up in an email scandal  resigned in disgrace an investigation  revealed racist sexist and homophobic  language used in emails to a team  executive a decade ago  another driver is in trouble for driving  right through the middle of the henry  rugs crime scene our camera was rolling  when that driver blew past metro police  vehicles coming dangerously close to the  cars involved officers quickly  surrounded that suv the driver was cited  police want to remind everyone to never  drive through the scene of an active  investigation and we are continuing to  follow the arrest of henry ruggs we're  also working to find out more about the  victims in this crash and you can follow  the latest here on air and online at  8newsnow.com  good afternoon everyone ted florento  here with your weather now another  beautiful day outside the clouds have  cleared air quality also in the good  range temperatures perfect for this fall  november day in the mid 70s at this hour  winds are staying light and calm after  those elevated winds we had yesterday  one shouldn't be an issue for tonight  either in fact here's your evening  planner we'll increase the cloud